{{Quote|Perhaps all Kowakian monkey-lizards should be exterminated for the good of the galaxy.|Count Dooku|<ref name="Dooku Captured (short story)">{{StoryCite|story=Dooku Captured (short story)|book=The Clone Wars: Stories of Light and Dark}}</ref>}}
'''Kowakian monkey-lizards''', also known as '''Kowakians''', were a race of [[Sentience|semi-sentient]] [[Reptile|reptilian]] creatures often used by members of the underworld as pets. Owners of Kowakians included [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure]],<ref name="Episode VI" /> [[Hondo Ohnaka]],<ref name="Dooku Captured" /> and [[Emil Graf]].<ref name="The Escape">''[[Adventures in Wild Space: The Escape]]''</ref> They were capable of using weapons such as a [[blaster]] and, in the case of [[Pikk Mukmuk]], a [[pirate]] [[WLO-5 speeder tank|tank]].<ref name="Bounty Hunters" /> [[Unidentified Kowakian monkey-lizard bounty hunter|One Kowakian]] became a [[bounty hunter]] and turned the [[Wookiee]] [[Chewbacca]] over to the [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="Junior Novel">''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story: A Junior Novel]]''</ref> They were related to the much larger [[Kowakian ape-lizard]].<ref name="Buckets list">{{SW|url=news/buckets-list-extra-signal-from-sector-six-star-wars-resistance|text=Bucket's List Extra: 10 Fun Facts from "Signal from Sector Six" - ''Star Wars Resistance''}}</ref> Due to their appearance they were often mistaken for pests.<ref name="VE">''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''</ref> Monkey-lizards were quite intelligent and capable of mimicking almost any language.<ref name="Kowakian GoC" />

==Biology and appearance==
The impish Kowakian monkey-lizards,<ref name="Kowakian Monkey-Lizard" /> simply referred to as Kowakians,<ref name="TGG EF OG">{{SWArchive|url=theclonewars/guide/episode012.html|text=''The Clone Wars'' Episode Guide: The Gungan General}}</ref> were a [[species]] of [[Sentience|semi-sentient]]<ref name="Helmet Collection 12" /> [[Reptile|reptilian]].<ref name="Kowakian GoC" /> Kowakian monkey-lizards had [[Color|multihued]] skin, including red,<ref name="Kowakian Monkey-Lizard" /> blue, yellow, brown, green, purple, and orange.<ref name="Kowakian GoC" /> Their average height ranged from fifty-eight to seventy [[centimeter]]s, with an average weight of twelve [[kilogram]]s. Their diets included [[insect]]s, [[worm]]s, and small [[rodent]]s.<ref name="Bestiary" />

==Behavior and intelligence==
The species was known for their shrill laughter and sophisticated senses of humor.<ref name="Kowakian Monkey-Lizard" /> They were often caught stealing and taunting unsuspecting bypassers.<ref name="Bestiary" /> However, despite their mischievous nature, Kowakian monkey-lizards could give their respects and be befriended if someone managed to match their senses of humor.<ref name="Kowakian GoC" /> The Kowakians had natural curiosity and high intelligence,<ref name="Bestiary" /> being able to repair a [[starship]],<ref name="Kowakian GoC" /> commandeer a [[tank]], wield a [[blaster]], and mimic most [[language]]s, including [[Huttese]] and [[Galactic Basic Standard|Galactic Basic]]. While they were able to mimic languages, the Kowakian monkey-lizards primarily communicate through their jubilant laughter.<ref name="Bestiary" />

==History==
Kowakian monkey-lizards hailed from the [[planet]] [[Kowak]].<ref name="Kowakian Monkey-Lizard" />

==Kowakians in the galaxy==
{{Quote|Kowakian monkey lizards&mdash;biggest pain this side of the galaxy. I hate those things! Hate 'em!|Poe Dameron|<ref name="Signal from Sector Six">{{Resistance|Signal from Sector Six}}</ref>}}
[[File:PilfMukmukRelic-SWGoH.png|thumb|left|250px|Pilf Mukmuk, a red Kowakian monkey-lizard]]
A notable Kowakian monkey-lizard was [[Salacious B. Crumb]], who served as court [[Jester (occupation)|jester]] in [[Boba Fett's Palace|Jabba's Palace]] during the [[Imperial Era|reign]] of the [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="Salacious B. Crumb">{{Databank|salacious-crumb|Salacious B. Crumb}}</ref> By [[3 ABY]],<ref name="OutlawsDate">{{OutlawsDate}}</ref> the monkey-lizards had been accidentally introduced to the ecosystem of [[Akiva]]. Due to their ability to live off almost any type of sustenance, their population increased drastically on the planet. The Akivan monkey-lizards would seek out settlements and travelers in the planet's jungles to steal their food and valuables. When [[thief]] [[Kay Vess]] approached [[Research Station 57]], she was attacked by a monkey-lizard that threw objects at her from a tree.<ref name="Outlaws">''[[Star Wars Outlaws]]''</ref>

In [[9 ABY]],<ref name="Date">{{MandoDate|3}}</ref> [[roasted Kowakian monkey-lizard]]s was a [[Foodstuff|food]] item sold at a [[Nevarro bazaar|bazaar]]<ref name="Chapter 3">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 3: The Sin}}</ref> within [[Nevarro City]]<ref name="SWCE">Star Wars: Character Encyclopedia, Updated and Expanded Edition</ref> on the planet<ref name="Nevarro DB">{{Databank|nevarro|Nevarro}}</ref> [[Nevarro]]. When [[bounty hunter]] [[Din Djarin]] arrived at the city, he passed a roasted monkey lizard stand, where a still-living Kowakian monkey-lizard, caged, looked out in fear.<ref name="Chapter 3" /> Sometime later, as Nevarro City improved and became more respectable under the leadership of [[High Magistrate]] [[Greef Karga]], several Kowakian monkey-lizards resided peacefully on trees within the city, and were no longer being roasted.<ref name="Chapter 17">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 17: The Apostate}}</ref>

In [[34 ABY]],<ref name="Date Note">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of "[[The Voxx Vortex 5000]]" to [[34 ABY]].</ref> several [[Color|olive brown]] monkey-lizards worked in [[Vranki]] the Blue's [[Vranki's Hotel and Casino|Hotel and Casino]], wearing a uniform of a small blue hat and an orange collar and performing various tasks, including fetching items for [[Vranki]]. They attacked [[Neeku Vozo]], a visiting resident of the ''[[Colossus]]'', when they discovered he was giving instructions to [[Kazuda Xiono]] to give him a better chance at winning his race against [[Team Vranki]]. They knocked the [[datapad]] Vozo was using to observe the course out of his hands, and he was so preoccupied with fighting them off that he was unable to give Xiono warnings about several obstacles. Despite the monkey-lizards' attempts to distract him, Vozo was able to turn off the finish hoop's [[laser cannon]]s, which enabled Xiono to win the race. Even after the end of the race, they continued to attack Vozo, although they eventually allowed him to leave with the rest of the Colossus residents.<ref name="Voxx Vortex 5000">{{Resistance|The Voxx Vortex 5000}}</ref>

Around [[34 ABY]], Kowakian monkey-lizards were imported to the planet [[Batuu]] and sold as pets in the [[Creature Stall]] at [[Black Spire Outpost]].<ref name="Galaxy'sEdge">{{GEAttr|Creature Stall}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
Kowakian monkey-lizard, albeit unidentified, first appeared in the<ref name="Episode VI" /> [[1983]]<ref name="Year by Year">''[[Star Wars Year By Year: A Visual History, Updated and Expanded Edition]]''</ref> theatrical film [[Star Wars: Episode VI Return of the Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VI ''Return of the Jedi'']].<ref name="Episode VI" /> The original [[StarWars.com]] episode guide for "[[Shadow of Malevolence|Shadow of ''Malevolence'']]"&mdash;the [[The Clone Wars: Season One|first season]]'s third episode of the animated series ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]''&mdash;reintroduced the species' name to [[canon]], though it was missing the hyphen,<ref name="SoM EG OG">{{SWArchive|url=theclonewars/guide/episode003.html|text=''The Clone Wars'' Episode Guide: Shadow of ''Malevolence''}}</ref> which the modern episode guide of the same episode would later correct.<ref name="SoM EG New">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/shadow-of-malevolence-episode-guide|text="Shadow of Malevolence" Episode Guide &#124; The Clone Wars}}</ref> The species was later identified as just "Kowakian" in the original episode guide for "[[The Gungan General]]," the first season's twelfth episode of ''Star Wars: The Clone Wars''.<ref name="TGG EF OG">{{SWArchive|url=theclonewars/guide/episode012.html|text=''The Clone Wars'' Episode Guide: The Gungan General}}</ref>

In the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, the species was first identified as the [[Kowakian monkey-lizard/Legends|Kowakian monkey-lizard]] via ''[[Galaxy Guide 5: Return of the Jedi]]'', a supplement for the ''[[Star Wars: The Roleplaying Game]]'' written by [[Michael Stern]] and published by [[West End Games]]<ref name="GG5">''[[Galaxy Guide 5: Return of the Jedi]]''</ref> in [[January]] [[1990]].<ref name="Lucasfilm">''Galaxy Guide 5: Return of the Jedi'' first appears in the product listings of ''[[The Lucasfilm Fan Club Magazine 10]]'', released in [[January]] [[1990]].</ref>

